Analyze the following flawed Node.js async event dispatcher implementation:
```javascript
class AsyncQueueDispatcher {
  constructor() {
    this.listeners = {};
    this.queue = [];
    this.processing = false;
  }
  on(event, handler) {
    if (!this.listeners[event]) this.listeners[event] = [];
    this.listeners[event].push(handler);
  }
  off(event, handler) {
    this.listeners[event] = this.listeners[event].filter(h => h !== handler);
  }
  async emit(event, data) {
    this.queue.push({ event, data });
    if (this.processing) return;
    this.processing = true;
    while (this.queue.length > 0) {
      const item = this.queue.shift();
      const handlers = this.listeners[item.event] || [];
      for (const h of handlers) {
        h(item.data);
      }
    }
    this.processing = false;
  }
}
```
Identify four distinct bugs: 1) Unhandled asynchronous rejections when a handler returns a rejected Promise; 2) Race condition when emit() is called during an asynchronous handler execution; 3) Memory leak when `off()` is called on empty listener arrays; and 4) Event listener array mutation while iterating during handler unregistration. Provide the fully corrected, production-hardened implementation with concurrency safety.

execution.finalAnswer:
Is implementation mein kuch important issues hain. Sabse pehle, handlers asynchronous ho sakte hain par aapka loop unka wait nahi kar raha, jisse race conditions aur unhandled promise rejections ka risk hota hai. Dusra, listeners array ko iterate karte waqt off method se mutation hone par errors aa sakte hain, aur off method empty arrays ka check nahi karta. Yeh raha ek production-hardened version jo concurrency aur robustness handle karta hai: javascript
class AsyncQueueDispatcher { constructor() { this.listeners = new Map(); this.queue = []; this.processing = false; } on(event, handler) { if (!this.listeners.has(event)) this.listeners.set(event, []); this.listeners.get(event).push(handler); } off(event, handler) { const handlers = this.listeners.get(event); if (!handlers) return; // Mutation safety ke liye filter ka use aur cleanup const nextHandlers = handlers.filter(h = h !== handler); if (nextHandlers.length === 0) { this.listeners.delete(event); } else { this.listeners.set(event, nextHandlers); } } async emit(event, data) { this.queue.push({ event, data }); if (this.processing) return; this.processing = true; try { while (this.queue.length 0) { const { event, data } = this.queue.shift(); const handlers = this.listeners.get(event); if (handlers) { // Snapshot banaya taki loop ke dauran mutation safe rahe const snapshot = [...handlers]; // Promise.all se concurrency aur errors handle kiye await Promise.all(snapshot.map(async (h) = { try { await h(data); } catch (err) { console.error(Error in listener for {event}:, err); } })); } } } finally { this.processing = false; } }
} Is version mein maine Map ka use kiya hai aur Promise.all ke saath try-catch lagaya hai taaki ek faulty handler pure queue ko block na kare. Saath hi, snapshot banane se iteration ke dauran listener list badalne par koi issue nahi hoga.
